  "worked_solution": "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=2\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\theta )$, ${\\theta }_{1}=0$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\pi $, this gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(2\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\theta ))^{2}\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
